1
00:00:14,139 --> 00:00:15,557
Keep going.

2
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:18,893
- Back!
- Which one are you talking about, Weather?

3
00:00:19,728 --> 00:00:22,731
Is it Jolyne, who you think
is already near the hospital?

4
00:00:22,814 --> 00:00:25,734
Or… do you mean the priest is nearby?

5
00:00:25,817 --> 00:00:28,987
No, it's all three, Anastasia.

6
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:31,948
Jolyne, the priest, and another enemy.

7
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:33,867
I feel all three of them.

8
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:36,286
Find them. Where are they?

9
00:00:36,369 --> 00:00:38,288
Are they inside the building?

10
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:42,083
Attention all passengers.

11
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:49,174
It is July 21, 2005,
and time to destination is 21:33.

12
00:00:49,257 --> 00:00:51,134
This aircraft will crash to the ground.

13
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:54,929
TWO MINUTES UNTIL CRASH

14
00:00:56,765 --> 00:00:58,933
What the hell are you doing?

15
00:00:59,017 --> 00:01:01,144
Why are you messing with that door?

16
00:01:01,227 --> 00:01:03,730
We can't find the exit on the ceiling.

17
00:01:03,813 --> 00:01:08,151
The fastest way to get out
is to defeat the Stand User.

18
00:01:09,486 --> 00:01:11,905
Ermes, hold onto my thread again.

19
00:01:11,988 --> 00:01:13,907
Grab onto to a fixture.

20
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:15,658
You, flight attendant,

21
00:01:15,742 --> 00:01:18,369
go change the door to manual mode.

22
00:01:18,453 --> 00:01:20,371
What? Hold on.

23
00:01:20,455 --> 00:01:24,375
Isn't it dangerous to open
the door mid-flight?

24
00:01:24,459 --> 00:01:25,502
Doesn't the air pressure…

25
00:01:30,131 --> 00:01:31,424
No.

26
00:01:32,008 --> 00:01:33,510
Go!

27
00:01:33,593 --> 00:01:36,805
She's riding the airflow
to strike the User!

28
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:45,438
Mayday!

29
00:01:45,522 --> 00:01:48,149
Took a hit from a MiG.

30
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:49,526
Lost control of the aircraft.

31
00:01:50,109 --> 00:01:52,278
This is coming to a close fast.

32
00:01:52,362 --> 00:01:54,948
Who are you?

33
00:01:55,490 --> 00:01:59,202
Doesn't matter.
Looks like the back seat was compromised.

34
00:01:59,285 --> 00:02:01,913
Check the damage for me, will you?

35
00:02:01,996 --> 00:02:03,039
What's this?

36
00:02:14,968 --> 00:02:16,970
Fuck!

37
00:02:17,679 --> 00:02:19,139
Jolyne!

38
00:02:19,722 --> 00:02:21,349
Stone Ocean!

39
00:02:23,268 --> 00:02:25,103
McCoy on the line.

40
00:02:25,186 --> 00:02:26,813
We just arrived at the scene.

41
00:02:27,355 --> 00:02:31,109
This is incomprehensible,
but there's a hole in a patient's room.

42
00:02:31,192 --> 00:02:32,443
Its depth is unknown.

43
00:02:34,195 --> 00:02:37,532
Jolyne Cujoh learned how to fight
in prison.

44
00:02:38,116 --> 00:02:42,328
She foresaw that
her launched attack would fail.

45
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:44,998
She left the plane for the walkie-talkie.

46
00:02:45,081 --> 00:02:47,584
She waited for the police
to arrive at the scene.

47
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:50,962
She knew the officers would bring radios.

48
00:02:51,045 --> 00:02:53,131
She will call her ally now.

49
00:02:53,214 --> 00:02:57,051
The frequency on those talkies
can be adjusted to dial cell phones.

50
00:02:57,135 --> 00:02:59,846
Can't you just shut up for a moment?

51
00:02:59,929 --> 00:03:02,223
Does it look like I'm losing?

52
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:07,103
Tell me, Father. Who's winning?

53
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:43,199
I grew up not knowing who my father was.

54
00:04:43,783 --> 00:04:48,871
I got sick of my mother and stepfather
who doted on my stepsisters,

55
00:04:48,955 --> 00:04:50,456
so I ran away from home.

56
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:51,666
I was 13.

57
00:04:52,667 --> 00:04:54,836
I meant to be gone for a few days,

58
00:04:54,919 --> 00:04:57,672
and I was wandering around,
looking for a place to sleep.

59
00:04:57,755 --> 00:05:00,008
Just then, a pair of spikes
fell from the skies.

60
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:02,468
They were baseball spikes.

61
00:05:03,052 --> 00:05:05,013
They smelled very nice.

62
00:05:05,805 --> 00:05:08,391
Did someone toss them from a roof?

63
00:05:08,474 --> 00:05:10,435
It made no sense.
The spikes were brand new.

64
00:05:10,518 --> 00:05:12,979
They were sized 28.5cm.

65
00:05:13,563 --> 00:05:15,648
They were too big for my feet,

66
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:18,776
but I liked the satisfying sounds
they made.

67
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:21,070
I walked down the street cheerfully.

68
00:05:21,904 --> 00:05:24,282
That's when the cops pulled over
and arrested me.

69
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:29,037
This is not a trial.

70
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:31,080
We have questions for you.

71
00:05:31,164 --> 00:05:32,206
Okay?

72
00:05:32,832 --> 00:05:35,501
Did you steal them?

73
00:05:36,085 --> 00:05:39,464
The shoes were signed
by the baseball player Ichiro.

74
00:05:39,547 --> 00:05:43,092
The pair was originally donated
to children with disabilities.

75
00:05:43,718 --> 00:05:47,388
The collectors would pay
up to 10,000 dollars for them.

76
00:05:47,472 --> 00:05:50,308
The theft was all over the news.

77
00:05:50,391 --> 00:05:52,477
I told her the truth.

78
00:05:53,061 --> 00:05:54,771
They fell from the sky.

79
00:05:54,854 --> 00:05:58,775
You should be ashamed of yourself,
stealing from children with disabilities!

80
00:05:58,858 --> 00:06:03,154
Go reflect on your actions
in juvenile detention!

81
00:06:03,988 --> 00:06:08,451
This judge sent me to juvenile detention
based solely on circumstantial evidence!

82
00:06:08,534 --> 00:06:10,703
My parents did not appeal the case.

83
00:06:11,537 --> 00:06:12,705
Four months later,

84
00:06:12,789 --> 00:06:15,208
the actual thief confessed.

85
00:06:15,291 --> 00:06:17,752
He feared Ichiro's spikes
would get traced.

86
00:06:17,835 --> 00:06:20,254
So he tossed them
down a ventilation shaft,

87
00:06:20,338 --> 00:06:22,924
and somehow the spikes fell onto my head.

88
00:06:25,051 --> 00:06:28,012
By the time my innocence was proven,

89
00:06:28,096 --> 00:06:30,223
my body and soul was already hurt.

90
00:06:30,932 --> 00:06:33,684
I couldn't even walk straight.

91
00:06:33,768 --> 00:06:36,437
Somehow, there was a hole
in the facility courtyard.

92
00:06:36,521 --> 00:06:38,815
I tripped on it and fell.

93
00:06:38,898 --> 00:06:43,486
There was a knife inside a plastic bag
buried in the ground.

94
00:06:43,569 --> 00:06:44,904
I stabbed my hand on it.

95
00:06:45,488 --> 00:06:47,740
You've done it now.

96
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:50,701
I was hiding that knife, dammit.

97
00:06:50,785 --> 00:06:53,246
The next day, a gang henchman
who was three years older than I,

98
00:06:53,329 --> 00:06:56,457
beat the life out of me.

99
00:06:56,541 --> 00:06:58,584
A doctor treated my wounds.

100
00:06:58,668 --> 00:07:01,170
Yet two weeks later,

101
00:07:01,254 --> 00:07:03,589
bloody pus and a worm gushed out.

102
00:07:03,673 --> 00:07:06,425
I also almost died from a terrible fever.

103
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:09,053
Since that day,

104
00:07:09,137 --> 00:07:13,057
I hid from society
and started to live a tiresome life.

105
00:07:13,641 --> 00:07:16,018
One time, I pissed next to a trash bin.

106
00:07:16,102 --> 00:07:18,229
The walls crumbled down,

107
00:07:18,312 --> 00:07:21,566
and a woman's skull showed itself
from the walls.

108
00:07:21,649 --> 00:07:23,609
And now,

109
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:28,072
I finally understand
the cause of my bizarre life.

110
00:07:28,739 --> 00:07:31,701
It was my ability, Netherworld!

111
00:07:32,577 --> 00:07:36,038
Yes, at last,
my ability is under control, 

112
00:07:36,122 --> 00:07:40,126
but does this mean
I'm indebted to Father Pucchi?

113
00:07:40,751 --> 00:07:41,586
No.

114
00:07:42,378 --> 00:07:46,299
My father Dio's blood
runs through my veins.

115
00:07:46,883 --> 00:07:47,842
Father Pucchi,

116
00:07:47,925 --> 00:07:50,720
what makes you so much better than me?

117
00:07:51,304 --> 00:07:54,724
I can throw you into that plane.

118
00:07:55,349 --> 00:07:59,061
I haven't had a single slip-up.
Not even one!

119
00:07:59,145 --> 00:08:02,899
He rams through with his decisions,
just like that old hag of a judge.

120
00:08:02,982 --> 00:08:06,027
I'm getting really pissed at him.

121
00:08:07,361 --> 00:08:09,989
I, Versus, am invincible.

122
00:08:10,072 --> 00:08:12,742
Nothing is impossible with Netherworld!

123
00:08:20,458 --> 00:08:22,960
What makes him so special?

124
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:26,339
What if I present myself instead of him
on the new moon?

125
00:08:27,215 --> 00:08:31,302
Can I inherit the power
Dio hoped to obtain?

126
00:08:31,385 --> 00:08:33,137
I have the right too.

127
00:08:33,221 --> 00:08:35,306
I'm Dio's son!

128
00:08:38,684 --> 00:08:40,811
It's Weather Forecast's memory disc.

129
00:08:41,437 --> 00:08:45,024
How can I use this to my advantage?

130
00:08:45,107 --> 00:08:48,694
I want the power to go to heaven.

131
00:08:48,778 --> 00:08:50,905
Jolyne!

132
00:08:54,450 --> 00:08:56,452
Emporio, pick up the phone!

133
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:58,079
Emporio!

134
00:08:58,162 --> 00:09:01,082
Hey you!
Tell me the model of this fighter jet!

135
00:09:01,165 --> 00:09:03,251
How do I eject?

136
00:09:03,334 --> 00:09:05,920
The seat must be able to eject somehow!

137
00:09:06,003 --> 00:09:07,797
I've seen it in movies.

138
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:10,258
Tell me how to eject the seat!

139
00:09:10,341 --> 00:09:12,885
There's an ejection lever on the seat.

140
00:09:12,969 --> 00:09:16,180
But I didn't eject, you see.

141
00:09:16,764 --> 00:09:19,475
This jet crashed to the ground
before I could escape.

142
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:21,143
Those are the facts.

143
00:09:21,769 --> 00:09:24,313
No one can escape this aircraft.

144
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:27,316
Pulling the lever won't do a thing.

145
00:09:28,901 --> 00:09:30,486
What's wrong, Jolyne?

146
00:09:30,570 --> 00:09:32,446
It hasn't been that long.

147
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:34,407
Emporio!

148
00:09:34,490 --> 00:09:36,450
I'm inside a hole at the hospital.

149
00:09:36,534 --> 00:09:38,953
Ermes is on a commercial plane
that crashed years ago.

150
00:09:39,036 --> 00:09:42,039
I'm on a fighter jet.
We're about to crash!

151
00:09:42,123 --> 00:09:44,292
Search for ways to help us!

152
00:09:45,084 --> 00:09:46,085
What?

153
00:09:47,878 --> 00:09:49,130
Father Pucchi,

154
00:09:49,213 --> 00:09:51,382
do you have any use for Jolyne's body?

155
00:09:51,465 --> 00:09:55,595
The fighter jet pilot's body
was never fully recovered.

156
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:58,764
The impact obliterated him.

157
00:09:59,348 --> 00:10:02,101
Hello? Jolyne, take a deep breath.

158
00:10:02,184 --> 00:10:04,186
I can't tell what's going on.

159
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:06,105
I'll head back to the hospital now.

160
00:10:06,188 --> 00:10:07,732
No, Emporio.

161
00:10:07,815 --> 00:10:09,734
I'm stuck in the memory of the past!

162
00:10:09,817 --> 00:10:11,611
We can't change the crash.

163
00:10:11,694 --> 00:10:15,323
My survival depends on getting out,
but I can't eject!

164
00:10:15,406 --> 00:10:18,534
No, we're out of time.

165
00:10:18,618 --> 00:10:20,244
There's less than a minute left.

166
00:10:20,328 --> 00:10:23,956
The fighter jet will crash
before this plane!

167
00:10:31,088 --> 00:10:33,132
You flew the fighter jet into…

168
00:10:33,215 --> 00:10:34,634
You're right, Emporio.

169
00:10:34,717 --> 00:10:37,470
It didn't explode, Emporio.

170
00:10:37,553 --> 00:10:40,306
I rammed it into the commercial plane,
but it didn't explode!

171
00:10:40,389 --> 00:10:42,183
Of course, it didn't.

172
00:10:42,266 --> 00:10:44,310
The fact is that the planes crashed.

173
00:10:44,393 --> 00:10:46,187
So the planes will eventually crash.

174
00:10:46,270 --> 00:10:50,149
Until then, they won't explode
no matter what you do.

175
00:10:50,232 --> 00:10:52,526
- Jolyne!
- I'm back!

176
00:10:52,610 --> 00:10:55,529
Emporio, what should I do next?

177
00:10:55,613 --> 00:10:57,073
Let me see.

178
00:10:57,740 --> 00:11:01,994
It's Flight 2882 to Dallas,
a crash incident from six years ago.

179
00:11:02,078 --> 00:11:04,246
Miraculously, two passengers survived.

180
00:11:04,330 --> 00:11:07,124
I'm looking it up on my ghost computer.

181
00:11:07,208 --> 00:11:09,126
Go find those two seats!

182
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:11,754
You may not be able to leave the aircraft,

183
00:11:11,837 --> 00:11:13,964
but the ability runs
the exact course of events.

184
00:11:14,048 --> 00:11:16,592
You can survive by sitting in those seats.

185
00:11:16,676 --> 00:11:19,553
Emporio, hurry and find out
the seat numbers!

186
00:11:20,137 --> 00:11:22,390
That's Jolyne Cujoh.

187
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:25,643
She forges her own paths.

188
00:11:25,726 --> 00:11:30,189
Do you still think
you can finish her off, Versus?

189
00:11:30,272 --> 00:11:31,982
Shut up!

190
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:34,985
Who does he think he is?

191
00:11:37,696 --> 00:11:39,031
Found it, Jolyne!

192
00:11:39,115 --> 00:11:42,701
A newspaper article published
the seat numbers of the two survivors.

193
00:11:43,285 --> 00:11:47,415
They're Economy class, 51D and 51F.

194
00:11:47,498 --> 00:11:48,833
It's at the very rear.

195
00:11:48,916 --> 00:11:52,711
It also says that
the plane crashed at 21:33.

196
00:11:52,795 --> 00:11:53,629
It's all true!

197
00:11:53,712 --> 00:11:54,839
Run, Jolyne!

198
00:11:55,589 --> 00:11:57,675
The enemy Stand is here!

199
00:11:57,758 --> 00:12:01,929
It wants to get ahead of us
and destroy the seats!

200
00:12:02,012 --> 00:12:05,516
Thirty-two seconds left until impact.
This is a minor setback.

201
00:12:06,725 --> 00:12:08,727
I only have to destroy the seats.

202
00:12:09,353 --> 00:12:11,439
That's all it takes
to obliterate the fact.

203
00:12:14,942 --> 00:12:15,776
Ermes!

204
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:17,403
Secure the seats!

205
00:12:17,486 --> 00:12:20,781
We only have to sit in those seats
and survive the crash.

206
00:12:20,865 --> 00:12:23,075
Then, we can face the Stand User!

207
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:24,535
Let's make it out of this alive

208
00:12:24,618 --> 00:12:27,246
and defeat the Stand User!

209
00:12:28,372 --> 00:12:31,417
The seats are still intact,
but their attempt is futile.

210
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:33,836
There's only 21 seconds left.

211
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:35,421
I'll say this again.

212
00:12:35,504 --> 00:12:39,008
The only safe seats are 51D and 51F.

213
00:12:39,091 --> 00:12:41,302
Don't sit anywhere else!

214
00:12:41,385 --> 00:12:42,887
According to the article,

215
00:12:42,970 --> 00:12:46,056
all other seats were destroyed
in an explosion on impact.

216
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:50,311
It was a fluke caused
under miraculous circumstances.

217
00:12:50,394 --> 00:12:51,812
The two seats were in an air pocket.

218
00:12:51,896 --> 00:12:54,940
Once you sit down, buckle up.

219
00:12:55,024 --> 00:12:58,110
Guard yourselves with your Stands,
or you won't survive!

220
00:13:02,239 --> 00:13:04,700
Move! I'm taking this seat!

221
00:13:04,783 --> 00:13:06,911
What are you doing--

222
00:13:06,994 --> 00:13:09,079
Shut up and scram!

223
00:13:09,163 --> 00:13:11,040
You are nothing but recorded facts.

224
00:13:11,123 --> 00:13:12,500
No more than memories of survivors!

225
00:13:13,083 --> 00:13:15,461
You're not the people nor their souls.

226
00:13:15,544 --> 00:13:18,214
The real old man is alive and happy.

227
00:13:18,297 --> 00:13:20,799
Get out of my way.
Jolyne, we don't have time.

228
00:13:20,883 --> 00:13:23,052
Let's buckle up--

229
00:13:35,022 --> 00:13:36,982
Move, brat!

230
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:38,776
You're in our seat!

231
00:13:38,859 --> 00:13:40,319
Hold on, Ermes.

232
00:13:48,827 --> 00:13:52,540
Where the hell did you come from?

233
00:13:52,623 --> 00:13:54,792
This isn't my room.

234
00:13:55,292 --> 00:13:56,669
Where am I?

235
00:13:56,752 --> 00:14:00,297
I'm supposed to take my medication
after my nap.

236
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:02,258
You came down from the ceiling!

237
00:14:02,341 --> 00:14:05,261
Don't tell me you're…

238
00:14:05,344 --> 00:14:06,845
This can't be!

239
00:14:06,929 --> 00:14:10,140
They're not illusions, or even passengers!

240
00:14:10,224 --> 00:14:13,185
Where's the nurse?

241
00:14:15,312 --> 00:14:17,189
She's a real girl!

242
00:14:17,273 --> 00:14:22,319
The asshole pushed these kids
down the hole!

243
00:14:24,113 --> 00:14:25,531
What?

244
00:14:26,198 --> 00:14:28,576
No need to destroy the seats.

245
00:14:28,659 --> 00:14:29,952
Jolyne Cujoh.

246
00:14:30,035 --> 00:14:32,496
Don't forget to buckle up.

247
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:36,083
Go on, push them out of the way
and take a seat.

248
00:14:36,166 --> 00:14:38,919
That way, you two will survive.

249
00:14:39,003 --> 00:14:41,046
Physically speaking, that is.

250
00:14:41,797 --> 00:14:45,050
Once you crawl out of that plane alive,

251
00:14:45,134 --> 00:14:48,345
you won't be able to bear the guilt.

252
00:14:48,429 --> 00:14:52,433
Guilt that you sacrificed children's lives
to save your own.

253
00:14:53,142 --> 00:14:58,022
Will you be able to fight me
with so much guilt on your shoulders?

254
00:14:58,522 --> 00:15:01,901
You won't be so cocky then.

255
00:15:03,819 --> 00:15:07,948
Netherworld may not be
suitable for combat,

256
00:15:08,532 --> 00:15:13,120
but it can deal enough damage
to finish off such guilt-ridden fools.

257
00:15:13,203 --> 00:15:16,582
Jolyne? What's going on? Hello?

258
00:15:16,665 --> 00:15:19,543
What's happening? Who are you talking to?

259
00:15:19,627 --> 00:15:23,547
Dammit, the plane is beginning to shake!

260
00:15:23,631 --> 00:15:25,549
We'll put each child in our laps.

261
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:29,345
No, we'll all die.
Each seat can only fit one person!

262
00:15:29,428 --> 00:15:32,181
And there are three children!

263
00:15:32,890 --> 00:15:35,184
Are we in your seats?

264
00:15:35,267 --> 00:15:38,479
It takes me a second to stand up.

265
00:15:38,562 --> 00:15:41,899
Sorry, we'll get out of your way.
You can have your seat back.

266
00:15:45,694 --> 00:15:48,489
It's time. Two seconds,

267
00:15:48,572 --> 00:15:51,367
one second, brace for impact.

268
00:15:52,117 --> 00:15:54,495
Jolyne!

269
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:05,923
STAND NAME: SMACK
STAND MASTER: ERMES COSTELLO

270
00:16:19,687 --> 00:16:22,481
The victory is yours, Versus.

271
00:16:23,065 --> 00:16:25,526
But I saw three children.

272
00:16:25,609 --> 00:16:27,611
That's one too many.

273
00:16:27,695 --> 00:16:29,947
Don't you feel guilty?

274
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:33,409
No, it wasn't my fault.

275
00:16:33,993 --> 00:16:37,246
I was forced to do this
because Jolyne called her ally.

276
00:16:37,746 --> 00:16:40,416
Jolyne kept resisting
by finding the survivors' seats.

277
00:16:40,958 --> 00:16:43,961
Not to mention, I did this for you,

278
00:16:44,586 --> 00:16:46,088
Father Pucchi.

279
00:16:47,464 --> 00:16:49,299
Look, Versus.

280
00:16:56,223 --> 00:16:59,435
That's Ermes's sticker.

281
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:08,819
The surviving old man.

282
00:17:09,319 --> 00:17:14,074
The fact of the matter is
that the survivors didn't die.

283
00:17:14,158 --> 00:17:16,285
That's Ermes's sticker.

284
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:18,245
She copied the survivors

285
00:17:18,328 --> 00:17:21,206
and kept the children safe
inside their bodies.

286
00:17:23,292 --> 00:17:25,669
Ermes! That means…

287
00:17:26,378 --> 00:17:30,090
Where is Jolyne Cujoh?

288
00:17:31,341 --> 00:17:32,760
Ermes!

289
00:17:35,471 --> 00:17:37,097
Ermes!

290
00:17:37,931 --> 00:17:40,559
She lodged herself
in the body of the other survivor!

291
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:44,063
Dammit, Ermes!

292
00:17:44,146 --> 00:17:46,607
But Jolyne is dead!

293
00:17:46,690 --> 00:17:49,693
Jolyne has nowhere to turn!

294
00:17:50,277 --> 00:17:51,904
If I were you,

295
00:17:51,987 --> 00:17:54,865
I'd think this through more carefully.

296
00:17:54,948 --> 00:17:57,951
Asshole, whose side are you on--

297
00:18:13,258 --> 00:18:16,762
Jolyne unraveled her body into threads
as much as she could.

298
00:18:16,845 --> 00:18:21,308
She then hid inside my body,
surviving the crash.

299
00:18:21,391 --> 00:18:23,227
Good grief.

300
00:18:24,561 --> 00:18:27,940
Jolyne Cujoh isn't filled with guilt,

301
00:18:28,023 --> 00:18:32,361
but rather coming at you,
burning with wrathful justice.

302
00:18:32,444 --> 00:18:34,446
What will you do now, Versus?

303
00:18:35,989 --> 00:18:37,741
Netherworld!

304
00:18:47,292 --> 00:18:49,586
You won't be digging a hole

305
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:52,089
or excavating memories any longer.

306
00:18:52,172 --> 00:18:54,550
You're finally ours,

307
00:18:54,633 --> 00:18:56,593
Father Pucchi!

308
00:18:56,677 --> 00:18:59,471
Can I finish off the priest?

309
00:18:59,555 --> 00:19:02,057
Or should we do this together?

310
00:19:02,891 --> 00:19:06,520
Unfortunately, Versus,
it looks like you lost.

311
00:19:06,603 --> 00:19:09,314
Jolyne Cujoh's gravitational pull to me

312
00:19:09,398 --> 00:19:11,984
was much stronger than yours.

313
00:19:14,570 --> 00:19:16,280
Let's finish him off, Jolyne!

314
00:19:16,363 --> 00:19:19,867
This groundhog is done for!

315
00:19:20,742 --> 00:19:24,413
Weather Forecast!

316
00:19:30,669 --> 00:19:33,505
What the hell? What did he just do?

317
00:19:33,589 --> 00:19:35,924
Jolyne, finish him off!

318
00:19:37,551 --> 00:19:38,677
When did you take it from me?

319
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:41,471
Was it when Jolyne blasted you?

320
00:19:41,555 --> 00:19:43,015
Give it back immediately.

321
00:19:43,098 --> 00:19:44,766
It belongs to me.

322
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:47,936
You don't understand what you're doing.

323
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:50,480
Sorry, but I'm not going to die here,

324
00:19:50,564 --> 00:19:51,648
Father Pucchi.

325
00:19:52,649 --> 00:19:56,486
My ability finally awakened.

326
00:19:56,570 --> 00:20:00,699
I've never had anything to live up to.

327
00:20:00,782 --> 00:20:04,453
I'm finally starting to understand
why I was born.

328
00:20:04,536 --> 00:20:07,456
You don't understand anything.

329
00:20:07,539 --> 00:20:10,876
His memory must stay with me,

330
00:20:10,959 --> 00:20:12,502
at least for another three days.

331
00:20:12,586 --> 00:20:14,796
I won't end here!

332
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:17,424
I have the right to become happy!

333
00:20:17,507 --> 00:20:18,926
What are you saying?

334
00:20:19,009 --> 00:20:20,928
What are you guys talking about?

335
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:22,137
Jolyne,

336
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:24,431
finish him off already!

337
00:20:24,514 --> 00:20:26,350
It's too late.

338
00:20:26,433 --> 00:20:28,644
You can't finish me.

339
00:20:28,727 --> 00:20:30,896
He will regain his memory.

340
00:20:30,979 --> 00:20:33,273
I know it because I read his memory.

341
00:20:33,857 --> 00:20:37,486
He's not the ally you think he is.

342
00:20:37,569 --> 00:20:38,695
Memory?

343
00:20:38,779 --> 00:20:40,614
Is he talking about Weather Forecast?

344
00:20:40,697 --> 00:20:42,574
Did he throw Weather's disc?

345
00:20:43,158 --> 00:20:49,331
Weather Forecast is more than
a convict with amnesia.

346
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:53,669
He doesn't remember how his ability works.

347
00:20:53,752 --> 00:20:58,382
His brother, Father Pucchi,
sealed away his demonic powers!

348
00:21:00,133 --> 00:21:03,136
He is the priest's younger brother.

349
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:06,390
So Rikiel was telling the truth,
they really are…

350
00:21:06,473 --> 00:21:08,475
Weather Forecast and Father Pucchi?

351
00:21:09,101 --> 00:21:10,769
So you used Netherworld

352
00:21:10,852 --> 00:21:14,022
to read the disc's recorded facts.

353
00:21:14,106 --> 00:21:17,776
Versus!
You are nothing but a thatched hut.

354
00:21:17,859 --> 00:21:22,322
You have no place in the grand purpose
Dio and I have fought for!

355
00:21:23,031 --> 00:21:25,826
He's starting to remember.

356
00:21:25,909 --> 00:21:27,536
Look, he's here.

357
00:21:30,247 --> 00:21:34,167
Rainbows. There are rainbows!
The devil's rainbows!

358
00:21:34,251 --> 00:21:35,794
It's Heavy Forecast!

359
00:21:37,004 --> 00:21:39,381
Weather, what's the matter?

360
00:21:39,464 --> 00:21:42,092
Where's Jolyne? Why are you crouching?

361
00:21:46,096 --> 00:21:48,307
Weather, what's wrong?

362
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:49,474
What are you doing?

363
00:21:54,813 --> 00:21:57,941
What's your problem, punk?

364
00:21:58,025 --> 00:21:59,609
I was sitting here first.

365
00:21:59,693 --> 00:22:03,447
Don't touch me, I'll kill you!

366
00:22:10,537 --> 00:22:14,875
THREE MORE DAYS UNTIL THE NEW MOON

367
00:23:41,294 --> 00:23:46,299
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
